{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/184330-de-buff-style-hunter","id":184330,"title":"De-Buff style Hunter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-29T19:50:00-07:00","id":184330,"title":"De-Buff style Hunter","content":"So a friend of mine wants to make a character in an upcoming Hunter game. There problem is that theST we play with usually has creatures that he homebrews &amp; makes a whole lot healthier or stronger than they need to be, so straight damage is hard to do. My friend wants to play a character that causes &quot;status effects&quot; &amp; de-buffs to the enemy &amp; do them reliably &amp; have a variety of ways to do so, in case the Storyteller decides that his creature is &quot;immune&quot;. What is the best way to do this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:18:48-07:00","id":184483,"title":"","content":"Well off the top of my head, it sounds like your friend ought to be a clever guy with tools type.<br /> , <br /> Caltrops or marbles to slow it down, something to make loud noises to deafen, something bright to blind it, smoke to make it hard to see, or something to irritate its eyes, pepper spray type thing to irritate the nose, a net to entangle it, flammable liquid and a lighter to set it or something on fire, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T22:05:21-07:00","id":184536,"title":"","content":"Yeah, try to make someone that's say, Crafts centric, and then let em loose on making trap type stuff. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, De-Buff stylish characters I don't imagine really appear in the game because of how the system works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T13:13:06-07:00","id":185014,"title":"","content":"Since the Crafts angle is well and truly covered, some Endowment thoughts. What's your group's policy on homebrew? You could make combination Buff/Debuff style character with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/561-conspiracy-hakollel-shel-hamerkava-the-secret-names-of-god\">Hakollel shel Hamerkava</a><br /> <br /> Try the following Endowment spreads: Elah-avahati, Elah Elahin, El ha-Gibbor, El Olam, Elah Shemaya or Elah-avahati, Elah Elahin, or Elah-avahati, Elah Elahin, El Roi, Yhwh-Shalom, Elah Shemaya/<br /> <br /> <br /> Another option that probably won't work too well is to play a status 5 Lord Steward from Dream Catchers; the status 5 bonus allows you to grant yourself almost any Dread Power. But it doesn't last long and you can't do it often. <br /> <br /> The downside is that status 5 Stewards are deskbound government bureaucrats, sticklers for the rules, and don't like fighting. But mechanically it works quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T00:22:09-07:00","id":185399,"title":"","content":"She was thinking of using explosives &amp; Plasmic Caul (Fire) to protect herself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}